## 2. Put the obstruction inside any neighborhood

{{interactive_demo:1}}

Every neighborhood of $x$ contains an interval $(a,b)$. Choosing $\varepsilon$ smaller than $(b-x)/n$ for every natural $n$ puts every $x+n\varepsilon$ inside that interval.

