<details><summary>Reveal why compactness fails</summary>If a compact neighborhood contained the translated ladder, translation by $-x$ would give a compact set containing the closed set $S_\varepsilon$. That ladder would be compact. Every nonempty compact subset of an ordered topological space has a greatest element, contradicting the existence of a larger next rung.</details>

## 3. Why paths cannot move

{{interactive_demo:2}}

The surreal line is totally separated: any two distinct points lie on opposite sides of a clopen barrier. Since the continuous image of connected $[0,1]$ is connected, every path image is a singleton.

{{algorithm:2}}

